      "basis": [
        "Pinned1.1 limits675-677 defines the property as SampleMask array element count; minimum1 at2755. It is not a framebuffer attachment count or a general compute resource budget.",
        "Pinned1.1 interfaces2299-2368 maps sample32*M+B to bitB of 32-bit wordM and restricts SampleMask to fragment shaders. Existing admitted sample counts1/4 fit exactly one word.",
        "Matched IR3 load_sample_mask_in3118-3125 creates one-component32-bit system input (mask0x1), writes resultdst0; FRAG_RESULT_SAMPLE_MASK5387 marks writes_smask. FD5 emit714-747 routes one SampleMask output register to SP_FS_OUTPUT_CNTL_SAMPLEMASK_REGID and enables FRAG_WRITES_SAMPMASK, ignoring it only for single-sample. Native input/output representation therefore supports one mask word.",
        "Matched fd5_emit845-850 also writes fixed-function sample mask; a5xx.xml2079 supplies16-bit mask field. This corroborates atmost16 physical sample bits, but is not by itself used as proof of the shader32-bit array element contract."
      ],
      "execution_scope": "Hardware-backed mandatory scalar query correction. SampleMask is fragment-only and no exposed queue permits graphics draw execution. This is not a new graphics pipeline/compiler execution qualification; callable graphics-pipeline host behavior remains separately scoped, not converted into no-op success. No compute shader can legally test SampleMask builtin.",
